      "inputTokens": 157,
      "outputTokens": 1003,
      "costUsd": 0.0091055,
      "pronunciationText": "There's another way to see that answer. The graphs of e to the x and the natural log of x are reflections of each other in the line y equals x. Reflecting swaps x and y, and it keeps every shape the same size. So reflect our region. The curve becomes y equals e to the x. The y-axis becomes the x-axis. And the region becomes the area under e to the x, from zero to one. That's the integral from zero to one of e to the x, d x, which is e minus one again. So the pool's water has the same area as the region under e to the x. It's the same integral, with a different letter, and the strips now stand up."
