      "inputTokens": 163,
      "outputTokens": 1187,
      "costUsd": 0.0107645,
      "pronunciationText": "Now the region we couldn't do: under the natural log of x, from one to e, above the x-axis. In the pool, that's the concrete under the sloping ramp. Draw the rectangle from x equals zero to e, and from y equals zero to one. Its area is e times one, which is e. The curve splits that rectangle into two pieces. The piece against the y-axis is the water we just found, with area e minus one. The other piece is the concrete under the natural log of x. So its area is e, minus, bracket, e minus one, which is exactly one. The ramp's cross-section is exactly one square metre. We found an area under the log curve, without ever integrating the natural log of x."
