      "costUsd": 0.012186500000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Sideways strips have signs too. When the curve is to the right of the y-axis, x is positive, and the strip adds. When it's to the left, x is negative, and the strip subtracts. Take x equals y squared minus four, from y equals zero to y equals three. From zero to two, the curve is left of the y-axis, and the integral is minus sixteen thirds. On its own, that piece has x less than or equal to zero throughout, so its area is minus the integral, sixteen thirds. From two to three, it's to the right, and the integral is seven thirds. So, just like last video, the area makes each piece positive. Sixteen thirds plus seven thirds is twenty-three thirds. The numbers match last video's for a reason. This is that curve, reflected in y equals x."
