      "inputTokens": 120,
      "outputTokens": 768,
      "costUsd": 0.006972,
      "pronunciationText": "The same idea works for any base. Find the area between y equals log base two of x, the y-axis, and the lines y equals zero and y equals three. Log base two of x is the power of two that gives x, so x is two to the y. From an earlier video, a primitive of two to the y is two to the y, over the natural log of two. So the area is eight over the natural log of two, minus one over the natural log of two, which is seven over the natural log of two, about ten point one."
